{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement","id":1485044,"title":"Incoming judgement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-26T12:39:20-07:00","id":1485044,"title":"Incoming judgement","content":"Here's the context.<br /> <br /> I'm dm'ing a changing breed campaign, the characters are fera at the exception of one werewolf, which is the subject of this post. All lives around the french city of Lille.<br /> <br /> So Sargon is a fostern (rank 2) from the glasswalker tribe. He's a member of the local cairn, even though he rarely interact with it's members outside of meetings and other important occasions.<br /> <br /> He'd rather spend his time cultivating his network of supernatural contacts, which includes the other PCs, as he think that with the largest perspective, he'll be more able to do the right thing for the world.<br /> <br /> During last session, Sargon goes to a suddent meeting of the sept at the cairn. Following a vision and the pressure from one of it's elders, the sept was going to lauch an all out attack agaisnt the vampires (un)living in Lille.<br /> <br /> Problem, Sargon has nothing agaisnt the leeches, worse, some of his contacts(and, while he would never admit it,friends) are vampires. After trying to dissuade the elders from validating the attack, he's considered unreliable on the issue due to his contacts(a fact known to the sept) and ordered to stay out of the operation.<br /> <br /> Sargon decided to secretly messages his contacts to warn them of the impending attack.<br /> <br /> The following day, Sargon is convocated at the cairn, he faced the hateful gazes of the warriors, wounded and with two losses as the warned contacts gave the message to all vampires of the city, which were able to prepare themselves and ambush the garous.<br /> <br /> So at the end of the session, Sargon is detained at the cairn and accused of putting his brothers in arm in danger to protect wyrmlings, to have disobeyed a direct order of the elders. And many claims that his action was direct betrayal.<br /> <br /> So here I am, organising the next session, which will be his judgement.<br /> <br /> Considering his actions, what punishments would he risk?<br /> <br /> Things to consider: he will be judged by three elder: the sept chief, a fianna that allowed many transgressions from Sargon, but is out of patience with him, the elder that called for the attack, a theurge of the children of gaia, obsessed with the elimination of vampires, and a glasswalker, who many time defended Sargon agaisnt accusations of betrayal for his contacts with vampires that were formulated earlier in the campaign.<br /> <br /> With them will be the guardian spirit of the cairn, a being that manifest the concept of binding promises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T14:45:58-07:00","id":1485055,"title":"","content":"OK, I understand this probably isn't the best answer for keeping the game fun...<br /> <br /> But death. The Sept isn't going to be debating if Sargon is going to die, they're going to be debating how horribly he's going to die. The Garou are a military society and he gave vital intelligence to the enemy that cost Garou lives that was not part of an approved counter-intelligence operation. In war, you do that, and you get executed. In the eyes of the Garou Nation he's a traitor. He did something there's pretty much no coming back from.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that's before getting to the specifics of the Sept you've outlined, which all make this worse:<br /> <br /> - The Elders judging him are already in a 2/3s majority against him, and the one Elder that might take his side is going to be under immense pressure not to because in the eyes of the Sept all that time trying to defend Sargon's actions were misguided; if said Elder doesn't side with the other two to come down hard on Sargon, he's risking his own Rank and position in the Sept.<br /> - A Fostern disobeying an Elder is technically grounds for execution (if rare in modern times because Garou can't afford such punishments taking away their population). If he'd done this and no Garou died because of it, him not being executed would be seen as an exceptionally merciful ruling.<br /> - There's no way to spin this. Everyone knows what happened, and everyone knows why it happened.<br /> - A Caern Totem spirit of Binding Promises is at risk of abandoning the Sept if they do not deal harshly with a Garou that violates the Litany like that.<br /> <br /> And since he's already captured and awaiting trial... he's very screwed.<br /> <br /> Basically, you've left yourself two options: he dies, or the other PCs rescue him, and then he'll be declared a Ronin, his Rank will be stripped from him denying him access to a ton of things (spirits will stop teaching him Gifts and he'll only be able to learn them from his non-Garou friends), and he'll be hunted by the local Garou for the rest of his life unless he flees somewhere else, and even then he'll constantly run the risk of being killed by Garou who can then claim a reward from the Sept for taking care of their traitor.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you and your group handle things, but unless you're comfortable deviating significantly from the books here, or rewinding events to make things less harsh on him, events have gone in a direction with very few options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T14:46:22-07:00","id":1485057,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends a bit on your style of play. 1st Edition WtA had a different outlook on garou/vampire relations than revised Edition, for example. It seems, like the sept knew about his dealings with the leeches and at least tolerated it - something that would not fly well in revised edition, but seems to be acceptable in 1st Edition WtA.<br /> <br /> Despite contradicting circumstantial evidence in regards to specific vampires, there is no doubt in the minds of the garou society at large that vampires are wyrmish by nature, even if they don't know of the Wyrm or further Wyrm agenda actively. So, the attack ordered is beyond reproach and staying out of it is a direct order. The person issuing the order was, without doubt within the sept, of higher station.<br /> <br /> So, in addition to significant social stigmata and renown loss, there are two Litany tenets violated. &quot;Fighting the Wyrm&quot; is continuously not adhered to, but the sept has not yet brought judgement down on this, possibly because the character delivered results in the fight against the Wyrm in other areas. Failing to &quot;submit to those of higher station&quot; however is the more pressing issue here, and the circumstances are, that this cost the life of garou.<br /> <br /> So, besides any relatives of the fallen asking for retribution (there might be a Rite where a Kinfolk might be executing a garou in such a case) there are plenty of Punishment Rites that are applicable, and some that aren't a Rite. Banishment comes to mind, since people might not want to have anything to do with such a traitor (I mean, even when he opens his mouth, that might be a reason for a Rage roll by the packmates of the fallen garou). Also, since his words caused the death of garou, the Rite that changes the subjects voice might be possible, even though it is usually for liars.<br /> Being hunted to the death also could fall within the scope of what might be a suitable punishment. Really, the bandwidth is wide...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T17:00:56-07:00","id":1485065,"title":"","content":"Garou informing the enemy about an incoming attack by his sept, and that information resulting in the enemy killing an wounding Garou of the sept, constitutes treason in my opinion. The level 5 Punishment Rite Gaia's Vengeful Teeth is the most likely outcome after a very quick trial.<br /> <br /> Now if the information provided to the vampires only meant that those vampires escaped, no other vampires were informed, and the sept's raid was successful as planned, but the information leak was discovered anyway, then a lesser Punishment Rite would be more likely. Wanting to preserve one's contacts or informants is at least understandable. And while the Garou should not have done that without the sept's approval, at least in this scenario it did not cause casualties. In that case, I might choose the Stone of Scorn instead. At least potentially it might have caused actual harm (which it actually did), so a more severe Punishment Rite than the Voice of the Jackal is needed.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly OK for some Garou to maintain informants and contacts among the enemy. Glass Walkers and Shadow Lords are two tribes were this is more common. But this either needs to be done in secret or with the approval of the sept's elders. And it should not result in blowback. But a Garou disobeying direct orders to warn his vampire allies, who then warn the rest of their kind, and this results in higher casualties? That is not OK.<br /> <br /> Now since this is a PC, and you may not want to actually kill the character because of the negative impact on the game, you may want alternatives. One would be to subject the Glass Walker to permanent ostracism. Perform the level four Rite of the Lone Wolf instead. It makes the Garou a Ronin and outcasts him from the Garou Nation, with the idea that any Garou could kill him on sight and not be subjected to any penalty. Since the other PCs are not Garou, this would allow you to continue the chronicle with all PCs. You just have to make Garou NPCs very hostile to the one PC. The Player can then decide how he wants to proceed. Embrace being a Ronin? Start working to try to redeem himself? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T17:59:01-07:00","id":1485066,"title":"","content":"Jaysis. I'm in accord with Heavy and Black Fox, this is Death level punishment. They decided to be selfish, endanger their fellow Garou, went against orders, got others killed over their selfishness and did all that for a bunch of leeches. That's pretty much every wrong thing you can possibly imagine.They live long enough to be judged, they're not walking out of it. If they did, the dead pack's packmates would be out to end them. And the Caern spirit is one of Oaths and Bonds? That's just icing on the cake, his oath and bonds to Gaia and thir brothers should come before any personal entanglements. They trying to justify it by saying &quot;they were following oaths fairly given&quot; is gonna even put them in worse position, as they are not only a dangerous asshole that sleeps with the enemy, but is also actively endangering any Garou community (including the Caern itself) with an attitude like this and giving<br /> <br /> I can see that you probably don't want to be too harsh on the player and make them lose the character, but do keep in mind they have pretty much gone against all that the Garou stand for and there need to be consequences. If you do decide to let them off, I'd make it look like they're going to die until the last possible moment. Have them be assaulted by a near raging packmate of the fallen that needs to be pulled off him. Have their husbands, wives, children, brothers and sisters judging them with damning looks and cries for justice. Have the Judges of the Caern paint their crimes with the worst possible brush. They walk into this, they should be sure they are dead.<br /> <br /> Now you probably don't want to kill them, and they probably don't want to make a new character. I see two ways to deal with this at the end, either with a modified punishment Rite that has them executed by their kin or the pack that lost people due to their crimes - this could be someone disgusted by more killing, or someone who believed that the victim would want to give them another chance? OR... you said that the Caern was following the guidance of Spirits? Maybe the spirits or the Theurge that communed with them can interject before final judgement is passed. Something along the lines of &quot;Gaia has one more duty for Sargon before his Death, but the spirits never said we need to help him in that task, and for that reason we cast him out from the Eye of Lune and from this sacred record, striking his name from the rolls of the Nation and making his name a curse upon Gallilard's Tongues&quot;.<br /> <br /> Cue Rite of the Lone Wolf. Now, let's just hope that vague prophecy is enough that the packmates don't decide to get their own revenge on them...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T18:54:52-07:00","id":1485070,"title":"","content":"He is a traitor both to Gaia and the Nation and has conspired with the Wyrm to slay fellow Garou.<br /> <br /> Gaia's Vengeful Teeth seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T21:46:06-07:00","id":1485077,"title":"","content":"As others have said, death is the appropriate punishment for what he did.<br /> <br /> The best way for him to survive is for the other Garou not to learn about what he did, he manages to escape and go on the run, or the elders determine (in error) that he didn\u2019t contact the vampires. If he\u2019s found guilty, then it would be an outrage not to kill him.<br /> <br /> How did the other Garou find out that he tipped off the vampires? That would have been the easiest way to avoid him getting into deep trouble. At this point, maybe he could escape with the help of the other PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 06-27-2022, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T23:04:24-07:00","id":1485080,"title":"","content":"As a side note, if he does escape somehow, a nest of Nagah might end up in pursuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T23:21:18-07:00","id":1485081,"title":"","content":"For me the Rite of Lone Wolf would me more fitting. For a culture of warriors with strong tribal-social links death is more lenient (at least as I see) than beeing an outcast.<br /> But beeing a Ronin could also affect the gameplay harshly.<br /> <br /> By the way I don't think the &quot;save the character, because it's one of the player's&quot; is valid. Punishments shall be consistent on all level. If you let the guy escape without consequences, the game will loose some - and mayor - of it's aspects..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T00:23:06-07:00","id":1485086,"title":"","content":"Gaia's Vengeful Teeth seems inappropriate, I'd say. I haven't checked all sources, but iirc the Rite is for consorting with the enemy and actions/inactions causing many garou to die. This is arguably not the case here, the garou in question had friendly relations with vampires, but wasn't furthering their wyrmish agenda (most vampires don't serve or even know of the Wyrm) and his actions caused deaths of garou, in an combat situation that might have been aggravated due to the warning the vampires received, but it was a successful assault by the sept and there were inherent dangers.<br /> The Hunt seems more appropriate, since the garou in question had split loyalties (which the sept knew and tolerated up until this point, possibly benefited from in the past) and was put into this position by the sept. Under a Totem that follows the concept of &quot;binding promises&quot;. I think in was Jamie Lannister who at some point remarked that with all the oaths and duties you are bound to break some, for they contradict another.<br /> <br /> Ostracism is, like I mentioned, also a possibility. But, as with most cases, there isn't necessarily a fair or objective ruling on the matter, as the Truthcatcher also has to take the feelings of the sept on the matter into account, and these might be unfair towards the character in question. Garou are fanatics after all, so the septs reaction is totally understandable - just as their convictions lead them to believe the character convictions were just as strong and he would betray his contacts/informants/friends with his inaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T01:03:50-07:00","id":1485089,"title":"","content":"Gaia's Vengeful Teeth is harsh... but not out of bounds. In the eyes of most Garou this PC would deserve to be made an example of, and wouldn't see such an extreme rite as being anything more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-27-2022, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T02:07:34-07:00","id":1485095,"title":"","content":"I think the betrayal could have been worst but I feel from Gaia's Vengeful Teeth there is not much for offenders who do worst things (some more obscure punishment Rites not withstanding)....<br /> <br /> And sure, making an example out of a case is within the right and sanctioned by the law in many cases, but it contradicts the approach to have a fair or just penalty for the crime. For being made an example means that one person suffers especially to be a teachable example. So, the punishment doesn't fit the crime on purpose to 'scare everyone else straight', basically.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Gaia's Vengeful Teeth is outside the scope of possible punishments, though.<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder, if the garou states &quot;I had pre-existing obligation to warn my contacts, as you all knew, and the sept spirit's way is to honour those.&quot;<br /> After some frenzy checks there is an argument there that the sept potentially benefited from the relations the garou kept with the vampires and when the decision was made to attack them the elders specifically told the garou (adhering to their duty to inform a sept mate) but forbade to tell the contacts/informants/friends (basically ordered the garou to break a (possibly unspoaken) promise and acting against sept spirit's ways and personal honour). So, the sept put the garou on the spot and are now dissatisfied by the outcome.<br /> <br /> Hell, if a pack of high ranking Judges of Doom or Gleaming Eye Inquisitors were to show up, while that case was discussed and the tolerating of the garou's relationship with the vampires (for years) by the sept at large was made public, these sept Elders would be kicked back to cliath or worse in a heartbeat. For, if you let the Fostern play with matches, you don't get to be morally outraged if the house burns down.<br /> <br /> If the sept alone passes judgement, their anger and self-righteousness will surely lead to a devastating punishment for the Fostern.<br /> <br /> But like I said above, there is a shift in tone about vampire/garou relationships between 1st Edition and what came later. So, the way the troupe plays should factor in. Apparently the relationships with the vampires were okay-ish for a long time, similar to some 1st Edition sources...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T02:51:01-07:00","id":1485098,"title":"","content":"The shift in tone isn't really relevant because the big issues at had are<br /> <br /> 1) Disobeying a direct order from an Elder<br /> 2) Sabotaging the Sept's battle plans to attack an enemy in a fashion that radically changed things to the enemy's benefit.<br /> 3) Failing to uphold all his promises to the Garou Nation by putting his (possible but not currently stated) promises to some of the enemies first.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter which edition's view on vampire-werewolf relations, the three points above are all gigantic violations of Garou law. They'd be violations of Garou law back when Septs went to open war with each other and you betrayed your Sept to help an enemy Sept of Gaian aligned Garou. The fact that Sargon helped Wyrm tainted leeches is just reasons the punishment is going to be even worse on top of the base crimes committed. There's nothing here to make it better, just things that can make it worse. Even if you want to say the Garou Nation (which has no particular reason to come to the Sept to investigate the matter of a Fostern screwing up really badly and getting put down for it) gets involved, and they'd take the Elder's to task for failing to stop a Fostern from disobeying a direct order despite giving him a direct order rather than letting him skate by in gray areas in the past, that doesn't change is crimes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T03:16:30-07:00","id":1485099,"title":"","content":"Well, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> didn't yet state, how the attack went down.<br /> Were the garou who were killed really attacking a vampire who was warned, or was some Ghoul just luckily spotting the attackers and having silver bullets to boost?<br /> <br /> Disobeying the direct order, sure, is a beach of a Litany tenet but at it's core not warranting a death sentence.<br /> <br /> And sure, probably no external group would come in just for this alone - still if there was an external observation, the judgment might go down differently. If only sept members are present, an harsh punishment will distract anyone from failings by the Elders or by whomever might have been at fault in addition to the garou warning them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T05:04:52-07:00","id":1485103,"title":"","content":"The specifics of the attack don't matter. The Sept went from having the element of surprise, to being the ones that got ambushed instead.<br /> <br /> Disobeying a direct order regarding battle is absolutely something that warrants death if the Elder deems is so. The books have been clear over multiple editions that while death is not a mandatory punishment for disobeying an order like this, it is a valid one in the eyes of the Garou. There are many circumstances where killing a Fostern for disobeying a direct order isn't going to be a death sentence, but during something that clearly falls under the &quot;times of war&quot; element of the Litany that directly relates to battle is not where those circumstances live.<br /> <br /> As for external forces... which of them actually matters? Not even Jonas has the authority to just Moonbridge into a Sept and take over local Sept business because he heard some rumors. The Judges of Doom and House Gleaming Eye aren't recognized authorities with independent powers to act as they wish. A bunch of Judges of Doom showing up at the Sept to intervene can be told to go screw off and mind their own business and the Judges would have to be Athro or Elders to even consider challenging that, and they would need leverage do convince the Sept officers that any challenge they made was honorable. There's no law in the Garou Nation that a Sept has to allow the Judges of Doom in to enforce the law because they want to. They're not Interpol. They only have jurisdiction when Septs agree to let them have it.<br /> <br /> Outsiders would need to call for a Concolation, which requires five Elders of five different Tribes to all agree to it, gathering Garou from multiple Septs in the area, in order to force their way into Sept business. The threat of that is not enough to make the Sept care about what outsiders think when they have their own to keep satisfied. The rest of the Sept wants Sargon to pay for what he did from the description given. That's a much bigger concern than the idea that someone with enough power is going to care enough to use it just for this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T07:05:13-07:00","id":1485107,"title":"","content":"About the external parties, who could get involved, depending on the circumstances. We don't know the multitude of Legends and local tales that govern garou. Thing is, any Athro or Elder might challenge the local Elders. Even the fact that there are outside observers might change the behaviour of people.<br /> <br /> As for King Albrecht: he is nominally the King of all garou, which he usually doesn't invoke, but that is still commonly believed by many garou (especially since only readers of the Silver Crown novel know the truth about the crowns legendary power to just order any other garou).<br /> I picked Judges of Doom and Inquisition-type Gleaming Eye garou, because they are groups most likely making other septs affairs their business if they feel the need. A Concolation is a whole other matter.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd be interested what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> thought this might be headed at, and what the goals for his play are from here on out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T11:18:16-07:00","id":1485123,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for yoyr comments, it's been very usefull. In one hour we'll start the next session, I'll update you on the result of the judgement once it's over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T11:28:44-07:00","id":1485124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485077#post1485077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others have said, death is the appropriate punishment for what he did.<br /> <br /> The best way for him to survive is for the other Garou not to learn about what he did, he manages to escape and go on the run, or the elders determine (in error) that he didn\u2019t contact the vampires. If he\u2019s found guilty, then it would be an outrage not to kill him.<br /> <br /> How did the other Garou find out that he tipped off the vampires? That would have been the easiest way to avoid him getting into deep trouble. At this point, maybe he could escape with the help of the other PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer you, for a start, his involvement was pretty obvious.<br /> He was one of the few to oppose the attack, and his contacts with vampires were known, and suspiciously, the vampires were prepared.<br /> <br /> That made him suspect, but more damningly, the shadow lord of the caern, which is paranoi... Well, a normal shadow lord, has hacked Sargon's phone (in fact, every communication tool of the garous from the sept) and checked the records after the faillure of the attack, she found the text messages he sent to the vampires.<br /> <br /> And finally, Sargon didn't deny anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:28:14-07:00","id":1485129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485099#post1485099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> didn't yet state, how the attack went down.<br /> Were the garou who were killed really attacking a vampire who was warned, or was some Ghoul just luckily spotting the attackers and having silver bullets to boost?<br /> <br /> Disobeying the direct order, sure, is a beach of a Litany tenet but at it's core not warranting a death sentence.<br /> <br /> And sure, probably no external group would come in just for this alone - still if there was an external observation, the judgment might go down differently. If only sept members are present, an harsh punishment will distract anyone from failings by the Elders or by whomever might have been at fault in addition to the garou warning them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Following the warning, one of the contacts passed the message to the prince, a tremere who saw in that an occasion to show off his ability to protect his subjects.<br /> <br /> The attack was planned as followed:<br /> <br /> The habitudes of the kindred were recorded for around two years (including, ironically, with some infos from Sargon's contacts), two of the three packs separated to go two by two to the domains of separate elders and ancillae, disguised as mere humans pretending to be here to ask the owner for &quot;insert anoying bureaucratic mumbo jumbo&quot; then assassinate them.<br /> The third pack marked the &quot;communities&quot; of vampires that were outsiders, the gangrel living in the periphery, the caitiffs and thin blooded living in an abandonned factory, the anarchs in their turfs, and practice a systematic elimination.<br /> <br /> Finally, they were to join each others at 2 am to the elysium, block the issues, start fires and eliminate the leeches there.<br /> <br /> The plan was then to prepare to eliminate the next day the tremere chantry, as they knew it would require all their forces, then start a long campaign of purge of the underground and sewers for the nosferatu, as they knew that attacking them before would requires to control the entrance to the underground.<br /> <br /> That's the plan, in practice, the first two packs were surprised as their targets were absents, all the elders and ancillae were called to elysium.<br /> <br /> The third was surprised by a totally unexpected manifestation which blocked the entire place were they were supposed to attack and made them unable to join the others at the elysium.<br /> <br /> Finally, the original two packs reassembled at the elysium, again surprised by the absence of their brothers in arms, but decided to attack noneless because they might not be another occasion soon.<br /> <br /> They entered the merely guarded building, two unarmed ghouls at the entrance, and ended in a room under heavy fire of silver bullets, unable to attack the court who laughed at them, as the vampires were standing behind freshly painted anti lupine sigils.<br /> <br /> They had to retreat, two garous were killed in the fight, and of the other eleven, only one escaped without being armed by silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-27-2022, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:31:23-07:00","id":1485130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485107#post1485107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the external parties, who could get involved, depending on the circumstances. We don't know the multitude of Legends and local tales that govern garou. Thing is, any Athro or Elder might challenge the local Elders. Even the fact that there are outside observers might change the behaviour of people.<br /> <br /> As for King Albrecht: he is nominally the King of all garou, which he usually doesn't invoke, but that is still commonly believed by many garou (especially since only readers of the Silver Crown novel know the truth about the crowns legendary power to just order any other garou).<br /> I picked Judges of Doom and Inquisition-type Gleaming Eye garou, because they are groups most likely making other septs affairs their business if they feel the need. A Concolation is a whole other matter.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd be interested what <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> thought this might be headed at, and what the goals for his play are from here on out...</div> </div> </div> </div>I talked with the player of Sargon, he is fine with the risk of having his character executed.<br /> <br /> We are going to have the other players exceptionally playing the npcs of the sept, some defending Sargon, others condamning him.<br /> <br /> At best, Sargon might get exiled and become a ronin, at worse, of course, he'll get executed.<br /> <br /> It'll all depend of the way the judgement happens. I will update herr when it's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T22:34:42-07:00","id":1485169,"title":"","content":"Serious betrayal: death.<br /> <br /> If the Sept is made up by the most plotting glass walkers and others similar figures, they can order to have the leeches killed by himslef, then, exile him.<br /> But everything that would make him still a tribe member, or a living being, would be totally out of contest and illogical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 06-28-2022, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T14:13:29-07:00","id":1485207,"title":"","content":"Here's the update, we spend the whole evening playing the session, being reasonnable with the length. Okay, we *may* have been reminded of the external world by the apparition of Helios in the sky, but that's not important.<br /> <br /> So, the judgement was not very much in Sargon's favor, as you have expected. Howether, the glass walker elder convinced, at first, the others to allow a form of redemption.<br /> <br /> He &quot;pleaded madness&quot; so to speak, affirming that after too much time with vampires, Sargons was subtly wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of the other elders swallowed it, but they were not against finding a way to not kill Sargon without angering the rest of the sept (that's of course an info the players and the sept didn't have).<br /> <br /> They agreed on sending him, with an escort, to the realm of Cerberus, to be purged in it laked of molten silver.<br /> <br /> Howether, the child of gaia elder (you know, the one who hates kindred and asked for the attack) wasn't happy with otherwordly torture, she wanted the vampires to pay.<br /> <br /> So she agreed to sending him to Cerberus at one condition: Sargon must meet and murder his contacts amongs the kindred, to prove that he understand his fault, that his real loyalty goes to the garous and to prove that he desire redemption.<br /> <br /> So, happy (but torturous) ending right? <br /> <br /> Nope, Sargon heard the demand, and after a minute of thinking, straight out refused.<br /> <br /> He stated that he will stand by his principles, notably that he would not harm someone who accepted to become a contact, and for some, something like friends, despite the danger of working with lupines. And that if anything caused the death of the two warriors, it was &quot;the puerile vengeance of a deranged elder who cares more about settling scores with the undead rather than doing her job of fighting the wyrm&quot; and that i was because of incompetent clown hiding behind their rank like her that garous dies in useless battles and that Gaia is dying&quot;.<br /> <br /> He then proceeded to tell everyone present their home truths, things he knew thanks to his contacts, including the Bastet and Corax players.<br /> <br /> There was shock, outrage, dramatic fainting of a tightass kinfolk (he's a recurring joke of the campaign), many frenzy checks, many failed frenzy checks, and after calming everyone, including usingthe &quot;elder-slap-of-taking-the-younglings-out-of-frenzy&quot; technique, the three elders all agreed that Sargon should be executed. (The spirit of the cairn refused to give it's verdict, or talk to anyone, Sargon revealed too much secretly broken oaths from the caern members).<br /> <br /> You might have facepalmed yourselves reading this story, after all, Sargon had a paved way toward forgiveness and did the worse thing possible. (And as another player stated &quot;you could have accepted and run away while pretending to go to your targets&quot;) but it was epic for the table, it was daring, a satisfying conclusion to the researchs made by the aforementioned PCs on the sins of the sept members, and it made us fall into a dozen of minutes of endless laughting while roleplaying the drama following the revelations.<br /> <br /> Oh, and he nearly erased another PC from existence. At one point, he called the child of gaia, well, something I cannot repeat on a forum for fear of the banhammer, but it was so not expected that one the player bursted in laughters, spitting a whole handful of coffee on his character sheet. Which was miraculously saved by a strange technique of drenching it into water and drying it like an old photograph.<br /> <br /> Yes, we sometime think he's a legit magician.<br /> <br /> Back to the story. Sargon was condemned to execution the next day as the elder didn't want more garou bloodshed the same day the two warriors died (they died around 3am and the judgement happened in the beginning of the afternoon). So he was chained with silver in a caban on the ground of the caern until the next midnight.<br /> <br /> The corax PC, who spied the whole thing in crow form, warned the other PCs, a bastet and two ananasis.<br /> <br /> And they began to plot to save him before the execution.<br /> <br /> And they did so by using a tactic I've never seen in a dozen of WOD campaign.<br /> <br /> They called the police.<br /> <br /> And they told mostly the truth, they have a friend who entered a &quot;cult&quot; in the woods and after failling to prove himself by murdering people the cult deemed &quot;controlled by the dark forces&quot; and that they will execute him in the night.<br /> <br /> Of course, this being the world of darkness, the police would normally not investigate this, if only because of the leading officer was a kinfolk of the caern who uses his position to hide the actions of the garou, but said officer was &quot;mysteriously absent&quot; that day.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, the kinfolk is alright, although he might need psychotherapy after being attacked, bound in web, kidnapped and abandonned in the forest by a mass of hundreds of spiders.<br /> <br /> And the bastet finished to convince the leading officer in function using the eternal power of apparence 5 + &quot;crime agaisnt decency&quot; t-shirt.<br /> <br /> So Sargon and the sept were surprised by two dozens of armed policemen. The elders had to explain themselves to a famous character *probably* used by every people running games in modern day france: clich\u00e9 policeman with a south of france accent.<br /> <br /> No seriously, if you ever saw any kind of french comical movie with policemen, you know the character.<br /> <br /> Cue another laughting context, Sargon, understanding what's happening, play the role of a traumatised victim, and he's taken under legal protection. Of course, not trusting the ability of mere mortals to protect him from a bunch of garous, the group organised their extraction. <br /> <br /> And this is how it ended","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T16:09:43-07:00","id":1485221,"title":"","content":"Well. Nice of you to go soft on them. As long as everyone was having fun, it's fine. I'm curious, how far are they running away? I don't see their survival rates as very high if they do stick around in the area. Also was everyone but the imprisoned Garou out of the sept and noone was there who could handle the cops?<br /> <br /> And don't think I'm judging you for the choice you made in interpreting their play - I've gone and retconned things once in the history of my WoD games just to save the whole group because one PC was selfishly doing something horrible that implicated the rest so horribly they'd all probably be killed for what he did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T00:54:57-07:00","id":1485267,"title":"","content":"I'm probably misunderstanding...but to save to life of one traitorous chucklefuck they all knowingly compromised the safety of the Caern and Sept?<br /> <br /> If that Caern Totem doesn't call in every single favour throughout its entire brood to have them utterly destroyed I'm calling shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T03:36:37-07:00","id":1485272,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one of the few things even the non-Garou changing breeds tend to agree on: don't get humans involved. A lot of them are perfectly happy to mess with the Garou as long as it doesn't bring the heat down on their own kind, or put things sacred to Gaia at risk. Interfering with Garou justice is... iffy... forcing a Sept into devoting a huge amount of time and energy to make sure the police don't screw with the Caern is not going to make friends with even the most anti-Garou changers out there.<br /> <br /> I was expecting to hear that the other PCs rescued Sargon, because that seemed an easy way not to lose a PC but still ensure consequences.... but Sargon's tirade and the method of rescue just painted giant targets on all the PCs, and it's bad enough that they can't just move a few towns over and hope it blows over. Even other supernaturals that might be sympathetic and want to offer some help are going to have to weight that against a bunch of angry Garou, spirits, and who knows what else (the Nagah for example, think they exist precisely to remove these sorts of problems from the world) that might decide there's only allies and enemies in this matter.<br /> <br /> Everyone remembers the Wars of Rage... and nobody wants to start a new one over some Fostern Glass Walker that did all that... or his friends that decided to get murdered by Garou along side him.<br /> <br /> Still, if you and your group are going to have fun playing fugitives... it's certainly a big World of Darkness to try to survive in while being constantly on the run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T03:41:29-07:00","id":1485273,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NT-DKLDwm7g\" target=\"_blank\">I think this is what Nyremne was going for with the cops</a> So, we might have a tonal expectation mismatch if that's ok in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T04:36:01-07:00","id":1485275,"title":"","content":"As always: Everyone does at their table what makes their players have the best time. And I am happy for you guys if you had fun.<br /> Just for the sake of discussing a common ground in this forum, let me give a little feedback on how this would not happen at our table:<br /> <br /> Maybe you haven't seen this in a dozen chronicles because there are good reasons why noone did it yet.<br /> <br /> So now the mortal police (and any journalist or supernatural who could be bothered to have half an eye on what the local police is doing) now know about a &quot;CULT&quot; in the middle of densely-populated Europe, including the general area of the Caern (assuming the Sept didn't keep their silver chains hundreds of miles away from their meeting place _with the Caern Totem_).<br /> <br /> Police contacts (or contacts to people who are good at listening in into police stations) are among the most common backgrounds you'll find at any WoD table, so it's safe to assume that such an information source is also a pretty basic power foundation for any Vampire Domain, Mage Cabal, Hunter Cell out there.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cult&quot; is a pretty trigger word for investigative journalists, Hunters, Mages, the Technocracy, basically anyone...<br /> I mean: try the experiment and throw the information &quot;The local police had to look into an abduction by some cult&quot; to any gaming group playing any World of Darkness game and watch what the PC would make of it.<br /> <br /> Even if all the policemen turn out to be clones of Louis de Funes, you can't risk this kind of attention to a Sept.<br /> <br /> At least the Corax should know better than to mess with a Caern if you like to pretend to be in team Gaia.<br /> <br /> Edit: I just looked up the satellite photos of the region around Lille... it's one and a half hour away from Brussels and there are just buildings everywhere. There is barely any piece of nature left, let alone any forests big enough to hide a Sept when they want to howl at the moot without being heard in the next three villages simultaneously. You really don't want to be responsible for the inevitable snooping that follows, even if it's only local teenagers looking for that 'Cult' base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27469,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","user":"Ilsaena","date":".  I mean, it's Europe. 06-29-2022, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T05:59:05-07:00","id":1485276,"title":"","content":"Preface: Your game, your setting, no judgement. Just thoughts in general.<br /> <br /> I think Sargon should have been a ronin to start with, as he clearly seems to care very little for the Nation, Sept or even his tribe. He is putting the lives of his vampire contacts above the lives of his sept and so above the war of the Apocalypse. Are the vampires going to do the same for him? Or will he get a nasty surprise when they sell him out to their own benefit?<br /> <br /> In general, the party seems to put each other above even the Veil, as calling the police is a HUGE no-no. It is basically putting a bright red neon light saying to other supernaturals &quot;ATTACK HERE.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, it is personal safety winning over massive general harm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> One piece of advice I'd give for the future is to emphasise -why- doing what the PCs did was a very bad idea. The vampires might betray Sargon and where the caern used to be, there is now a toxic dump. Any kinfolk families are later found by BSDs and the Wyrmy forces start trying to recruit the party.<br /> <br /> Basically, if it fits your story, show how fragile the forces of Gaia are and emphasise how important the war against the Wyrm is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T06:41:49-07:00","id":1485281,"title":"","content":"There is always some suspension of disbelief around, right?<br /> <br /> If the Caern spirit is pissed because of broken promises by all the caern population the spirit might not even be around any more the next day. I mean, the whole problem with Sargon and the vampires was seemingly systematic for the whole sept. People have pointed out here, that Sargons loyalties should lie with Gaia, the Garou Nation, the Sept, the Tribe because they pre-date his loyalties / obligations with the vamps he befriended. But that is not necessarily what loyalty works like. I mean, why even tell Sargon about the attack and force him to make an active decision to break his loyalties or not when not telling him would have been the saver bet? Was it just because the CoG Elder was a dick? Did he think there was a teachable moment there for the GW Fostern?<br /> <br /> That said, spirits (even those acting as caern spirits) might choose to leave a caern. They have no divine obligation to save Gaia - or a single caern, only a vague need to help Garou due to &quot;The Pact&quot; (with various interpretations of the levels of adherence, scope, and other aspects, even within the game world). If the sept failed their part of the mutual agreement, the spirit is totally within its right to go, and has no need to be vengeful against the PCs. They showed that he was systematically betrayed for a long time.<br /> <br /> Sure, sending the police to a bawn is a huge gamble. And sure, it can lead to a lot of problems resulting from this. But it is the World of Darkness. Sure there are investigative journalists, the technocracy and so on. But there are also strange cults at every second street corner. If the technocracy with suitable manpower would go after them, there wouldn't be vampires, or garou, or Wyrm cults. Wait, didn't the Technocracy back the 2nd Inquisition.... maybe that is what we are headed for with W5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, a lot of garou will be very angry and possibly trying to get back at the PCs, but then again, they have to do damage control at home. Mobilise Gifts and Kinfolk to smooth over the legal problems the police raid might cause - fast.<br /> With Sargon gone and little evidence left, this might be relatively easy to accomplish. I mean, nobody wants bad press for the region. The vampires especially don't want to bring hunters or the Technocracy into the area, so they might try to take advantage but also will protect Masquerade/Veil.<br /> <br /> In the end, the sept might have to appoint another garou to fill Sargon's place as go-between.<br /> As occasionally stated books, the vampires are of the wyrm, but in almost any case the lesser evil compared to banes, fomori and BSD - so this is where the garou usually focus their efforts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T12:06:35-07:00","id":1485309,"title":"","content":"The repercussions of this should be massive. Sargon is now an escaped fugitive, and the sept has every reason to believe that Sargon's allies (whether they know it is these other Fera, or they imagine it was arranged by his vampire friends) purposefully endangered the Veil to arrange his escape.<br /> <br /> The Punishment Rites in general are only able to be used if the guilty Garou is present. But at this point, he's already been been proven guilty and sentenced. Having fled, I definitely believe when he is caught he'd be sentenced to the rite of Gaia's Vengeful Teeth. All the other Garou septs in the local area are going to be informed. There does not necessarily need to be some kind of manhunt to find him. Just all Garou have probably been informed of his crimes and given his description. If he's discovered, many septs will attempt to take him into custody or kill him themselves, while others may just spread the word about where and when he was seen. There may even be a concolation called at some point, and what the area's septs should do about the fugitive would be an agenda item. Sargon might even attract the attention of packs looking for glory by eliminating the fugitive, or Shadow Lords in the Judges of Doom camp.<br /> <br /> There's also the question about Renown loss, and whether a sept can cause it without the Garou being present. This matters because if the ST decides the sept can, there's probably enough temporary Renown loss to translate into permanent Renown loss that could affect Sargon's rank. He would have lost a lot of Wisdom Renown and a ton of Honor Renown due to all of his violations.<br /> <br /> This also brings up a question about Garou fleeing justice in general. If one can escape the typical penalties of Punishment Rites and Renown loss by just fleeing, and nothing bad happens unless the Garou of the sept (or another) can catch up to him, it creates a lot of bad precedent. There's a big difference between some scofflaw that avoids minor judgments, and someone sentenced to a major Punishment Rite who flees. Can the Garou really do <i>nothing</i> in the meantime before he's caught (if ever)?<br /> <br /> There are actually options.<br /> <br /> First. it is not necessary for the person who is the object of the Rite of the Silver Forge to be present. <b>The rite participants do not have to be in the presence of the target - all that is required is that the know the target's Garou name and be within 100 miles of the target.</b><br /> <br /> In other words, Sargon fleeing the Rite does not mean the Rite cannot be performed. The sept can carry it out anyway - presumably that very night once they escape the comical French police.<br /> <br /> Since it is very unlikely that the rite is performed &quot;unjustly&quot;, it should work. Therefore the next time Sargon steps sideways, he'll be sent to Erebus instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Sargon is ever released by Charyss in Erebus, he still has to answer for his <i>new</i> crimes in attempting to escape justice ad endangering the Veil, which will mean another (very quick) trial and sentencing, most likely the aforementioned rite of Gaia's Vengeful Teeth.<br /> <br /> Second, what about a hypothetical situation where the Rite of the Silver Forge was not the rite to be used, but one which requires the participant to be there? While the Rite of Silver Forge is an option if the Garou retains some hope of redemption, perhaps the sept does not want to use it. There is the ultra-rare Rite of the Shattered Soul, a rite only found in the first edition Werewolf Players Guide. It's even worse than Gaia's Vengeful Teeth, and the way it is written, it is not needed for the Garou to be there when enacted (though it's mentioned the rite participant through the dead's Garou body on the flames to be consumed - so this is something often done after the usual death penalty or killing during combat). Of course, being a first edition product, the rite as described is missing a lot of information that would be provided for the updated Punishment Rites. Any ST would need to make certain adjustments. It call spirits to inform everyone else in the Tellurian that the Garou is disgraced and no longer part of the Garou or Gaia, as he is an agent of the Wyrm. One of the things I do for my chronicles is say this Rite is held in reserve for lawbreakers in order to discourage nonsense just like this. Now there are some aspects of this Rite that many STs may not like (it states that the punished Garou will be reborn as a Bane), and it's probably why it was left out of future sourcebooks. But even so, I imagine there should be some rite <i>similar</i> to it that can be used against fugitives to discourage people from attempting to flee, or to encourage fugitives to return to justice. Such a rite would probably spread the world to whomever the spirits can, as well as inflict automatic Renown loss. No matter the specifics of such a rite the ST feels comfortable with, some form of that rite would benefit the setting precisely because of situations like this. It wouldn't need to be done in all cases, perhaps only reserved for major crimes. But it would be something I think some STs might like to have in their chronicles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T04:14:09-07:00","id":1485350,"title":"","content":"I always wonder how well known the Rite of the Silver Forge is and how well known the redeeming qualities of the Realm are. For most the trip is either a death warrant or a permanent imprisonment. I vaguely remember only few ever return and therefore only few bring back knowledge of the Rite that, iirc, is exclusively taught by Charyss. But that is just a side note.<br /> <br /> Renown loss is absolute. Storyteller guidelines clearly state, that even deeds nobody knows about shall leave a &quot;mark&quot; on the garou and be reflected in (temporary) Renown adjustments. Also, spirits can &quot;sense&quot; Renown. Not specific deeds, but a general gist (possibly separated by Glory, Honour and Wisdom, or other categories per Fera).<br /> <br /> You are probably right that every garou in the area will learn about these events.... unless the sept actively makes efforts to not let their failures become public.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean they allowed, for years, a member of their sept to have friendly relations with wyrm minions. Benefited from that. Allowed their operation to become a mess, because they did mis-evaluate the garou in question and his loyalties. Then they could not keep him until justice was met, but lost him and have a Veil threat on their hands, because they missed co-conspirators. Not the very best tale to tell in the neighbouring septs...<br /> <br /> EDIT II: I just though, since the whole thing with the sept and their secrets and potential breach of the ways of their caern spirit came to light, as well as the septs tolerance of Sargons ways on one hand and then to ask of him to betray his contacts so that the sept doesn't have to attribute this to their personal perception of honour, and all that.<br /> What if the whole sept and their downfall was a cautionary tale.<br /> What if Sargon was a Nuwisha to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 06-30-2022, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T12:00:34-07:00","id":1485400,"title":"","content":"OK... I get that you probably mean this as an attempt to offer ways to keep this specific game fun even if by not keeping too strictly to the setting and books...<br /> <br /> But the amount you're willing to stretch to paint the Sept as the Real Villains, and seem to think that Sargon should get immediately promoted to Legendary status rather than punished is... disturbing in its moral implications.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T13:07:43-07:00","id":1485409,"title":"","content":"Heinrich has been saying some things that I wanted to comment on because I feel he is assuming a lot that is not necessarily true, and if it is, should be very problematic. His posts have a lot of valid comments in them, but there's one thing that keeps coming up because I disagree with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485095#post1485095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I wonder, if the garou states &quot;I had pre-existing obligation to warn my contacts, as you all knew, and the sept spirit's way is to honour those.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485281#post1485281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because they pre-date his loyalties / obligations with the vamps he befriended</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485350#post1485350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and then to ask of him to betray his contacts</div> </div> </div> </div>All these quotes assumes one thing - Sargon has pre-existing obligations to his vampires that the spirits and the Garou have to accept. I don't think that is the case (and if it is, it's a major problem).<br /> <br /> First, what do handlers owe the spies they are handling? Usually the answer is nothing. The spy provides information usually for a reason - they are being blackmailed, hate someone and think this is how to get back at them, or for some kind of quid pro quo (I provide you the intel, and in return I get money or something else I value). The handler usually doesn't owe the spy anything more than what they are already getting. Spies - meaning recruited agents from the enemy as opposed to one's own undercover operatives - were usually abandoned and burned if they were found out. If they were extracted, it was usually to deny the enemy any additional intel they might receive, or to demonstrate to future informers that their side would look out for them.<br /> <br /> In other words, there isn't any kind of exchange of oaths or promises unlike the implied oaths that should come with a Garou joining the sept (even though this is something most STs and PCs assume rather than roleplay out and define). The spy is completely disposable and can be sacrificed (or risked being lost) anytime it is in the best interests of their handler's superiors. Handlers often sympathize with their informers. That's natural. They often advocate for them to their superiors. But it's because they have a personal connection is why making the decision to burn one is always done above them.<br /> <br /> So in most cases, someone like Sargon should NOT have anything like pre-existing obligations to his spies. Whatever implied obligations that exist in either party's mind shouldn't conflict with Sargon's actual obligations to his sept. That inverts the purpose of running a spy operation. Instead of them being his spies, he becomes their spy.<br /> <br /> Second, let's assume he did make actual oaths to some vampires. That would be sufficiently troublesome. Many septs won't have a problem if some Garou maintain some kind of contact with the enemy in order to gather intelligence. That does not mean they are sanctioning said Garou to offer oaths with them that conflict with their obligations to the sept.<br /> <br /> The most obvious response to a defense where Sargon talked about the oaths he made to a Wyrm minion should be, &quot;What????? Why did you make an oath to a vampire? When did this happen, and what specifically did you promise them? What other oaths did you make to our enemies?&quot; Those questions would not be to determine if Sargon is guilty, as admitting this just condemned him. It would be to discover the extent of the damage done so the sept knows how they might be compromised so they can take appropriate actions.<br /> <br /> Third, let's say Sargon's personal reasons override his duties to the sept, and he wants to save his informants. What is the best thing he can do? It's not what he actually did - tell them of the attack, because that might lead them to inform others (which they did). Instead, a better option would have been to say, &quot;Hey, something important has come up, and I have to explain to you in person. Meet me at this location at this time, and I'll tell you all about it. Once you're there, you'll know why I can't do it over the phone.&quot; Or something to that effect. Maybe it's not to meet Sargon, but some other important contact bringing the vampires evidence of something. Whatever is needed to convince them to go. And whatever time and location would place his informants far away from the scene of the attack. He's gotten them out of there to safety while not compromising any Garou plans. To not do this, but embark on a plan that exploded the sept's plans was a major blunder. And at some point, negligence can become criminal negligence.<br /> <br /> This is just a long way of saying that I don't accept that Sargon had any pre-existing obligations to his vampire contacts, and if he did, it was a big problem. And if his conscience somehow got the better of him, he had other options to &quot;warn&quot; his contacts without jeopardizing his sept's actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T13:52:52-07:00","id":1485418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> This is just a long way of saying that I don't accept that Sargon had any pre-existing obligations to his vampire contacts, and if he did, it was a big problem. And if his conscience somehow got the better of him, he had other options to &quot;warn&quot; his contacts without jeopardizing his sept's actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>With apologies to Nyremne, because I fully support their choice to make the game more fun for their group even if I didn't necessarily like the resolution.<br /> <br /> In addition to your excellent takedown of the whole spy and oath angle, there's a whole different tone in Nyremne's story about what Sargon actually thinks about the vampires. In the first post it's &quot;they're his friends even if he doesn't admit it&quot; and in the second post &quot;he realises that he's not going to fuck over his friends&quot;. Sargon is a very specific character who is setting his own personal preferences in front of his own Sept and Caern, he doesn't really care for them and cares more for the Enemy than he does for the Caern.<br /> <br /> Also (this may be a personal trauma speaking), but it seems to me that the player doesn't care about the implications or the cultural context, and was actually looking for a way to do his own thing and prove his attitude correct. I feel this is compounded by the willingness to actually threaten the rest of the cast due to his need to &quot;Fight the System&quot;. If he was an actual member of the sept, he'd have some kind of emotions and loyalty to them, as it stands, he was clearly out to show his individualism and devil may care attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:12:57-07:00","id":1485438,"title":"","content":"Well, I didn't expected such passion following the conclusion of last session.<br /> I'll try to answer everyone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:16:28-07:00","id":1485439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485221#post1485221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Nice of you to go soft on them. As long as everyone was having fun, it's fine. I'm curious, how far are they running away? I don't see their survival rates as very high if they do stick around in the area. Also was everyone but the imprisoned Garou out of the sept and noone was there who could handle the cops?<br /> <br /> And don't think I'm judging you for the choice you made in interpreting their play - I've gone and retconned things once in the history of my WoD games just to save the whole group because one PC was selfishly doing something horrible that implicated the rest so horribly they'd all probably be killed for what he did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think I went soft on them, the npcs acted in a way that was consistent with their character and the situation, the players took great risks and are clearly not out of trouble.<br /> <br /> For now, we don't know where they're going, we ended the session right after Sargon's situation, the players are discussing running away through the umbra, leaving the continent, or trying to find a spirit of deception to mask Sargon's identity.<br /> <br /> I'll also qay that I don't think I've retconned the setting or that the player of Sargon acted in a selfish manner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:18:25-07:00","id":1485440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485267#post1485267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably misunderstanding...but to save to life of one traitorous chucklefuck they all knowingly compromised the safety of the Caern and Sept?<br /> <br /> If that Caern Totem doesn't call in every single favour throughout its entire brood to have them utterly destroyed I'm calling shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Sargon is a garou here, the others are a bastet of the bubasti, a corax and two ananasis, the safely of a caern and sept of wolves is not high in their priority.<br /> <br /> As for the spirit of the caern, he has bigger thins to do, notably dealing with a sept that, he just learned were a bunch of promise breakers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:19:54-07:00","id":1485441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485272#post1485272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, one of the few things even the non-Garou changing breeds tend to agree on: don't get humans involved. A lot of them are perfectly happy to mess with the Garou as long as it doesn't bring the heat down on their own kind, or put things sacred to Gaia at risk. Interfering with Garou justice is... iffy... forcing a Sept into devoting a huge amount of time and energy to make sure the police don't screw with the Caern is not going to make friends with even the most anti-Garou changers out there.<br /> <br /> I was expecting to hear that the other PCs rescued Sargon, because that seemed an easy way not to lose a PC but still ensure consequences.... but Sargon's tirade and the method of rescue just painted giant targets on all the PCs, and it's bad enough that they can't just move a few towns over and hope it blows over. Even other supernaturals that might be sympathetic and want to offer some help are going to have to weight that against a bunch of angry Garou, spirits, and who knows what else (the Nagah for example, think they exist precisely to remove these sorts of problems from the world) that might decide there's only allies and enemies in this matter.<br /> <br /> Everyone remembers the Wars of Rage... and nobody wants to start a new one over some Fostern Glass Walker that did all that... or his friends that decided to get murdered by Garou along side him.<br /> <br /> Still, if you and your group are going to have fun playing fugitives... it's certainly a big World of Darkness to try to survive in while being constantly on the run.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think your depiction of anti-garou feras is accurate, from my reading of the breedbooks, the worse of them are in &quot;a good garou is a dead garou&quot; mindset","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:21:21-07:00","id":1485442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485273#post1485273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NT-DKLDwm7g&amp;quot;]I</a> think this is what Nyremne was going for with the cops[/URL] So, we might have a tonal expectation mismatch if that's ok in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for precision, the campaign is not comical or parodic, it's pretty &quot;base&quot; level of world of darkness, there's simply comical elements from time to time, generally npcs that have no real importance in the events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:24:29-07:00","id":1485443,"title":"","content":"Message deleted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-30-2022, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:26:14-07:00","id":1485444,"title":"","content":"[Message deleted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-30-2022, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:30:42-07:00","id":1485445,"title":"","content":"Message deleted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-30-2022, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:35:02-07:00","id":1485446,"title":"","content":"Message deleted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T21:04:03-07:00","id":1485450,"title":"","content":"Okay, I deleted a bunch of messages, seems making a one by one answer is not a good way to avoid flooding the thread.<br /> <br /> So for the big points:<br /> <br /> On the use of police:<br /> <br /> Yes, I know, the veil, and the PCs too, they acted in desesperation by making a move they knew the sept wouldn't have expected.<br /> <br /> It's clear that the sept and possibly the garous around the region will suffer high suspicion from the law.<br /> <br /> As to how the police was able to enter the caern without fight, there's a few things to consider<br /> <br /> -the sept had a kinfolk in the police, so the watchers always expect that if they see them arrive, they won't stop at the caern, so they were not so much alert to that<br /> -a good portion of the warriors were wounded with silver and not yet healed, making the idea of a fight less palatable<br /> -the sept was pretty incohesive following the judgement<br /> -the spirit of the caern went mute, and the theurges went in the penumbra to try to talk to it.<br /> -the caern really don't need to have cops disapearing near the caern, as someone mentioned above, the woodland around lille is little, it's not like you can hide indefinatly from eventual backup<br /> -the police received a pretty detailled description of the place and it's sentinels thanks to the corax who observed ot many times<br /> <br /> As so, the caern was really not defensible in this situation.<br /> <br /> On the debate on oath and obligations<br /> Sargon never made any kind of oath to vampires outside of &quot;you don't try to kill me, I'll do the same, wanna talk?&quot;<br /> <br /> He didn't acted on any sense of binding obligation, but simply because he liked his contacts and didn't wanted them to be a pile of ash.<br /> <br /> On the morality of the issue<br /> <br /> To be clear, I do not paint the actions of Sargon and the group as good or bad.<br /> <br /> Sargon did warn a group of dangerous supernatural beings that the caern would attack<br /> He did insult his superiors and every members of the sept, knowing full well that the spirit protecting the caern would react badly<br /> The group knew that involving the police would put the caern in their files for possibly decades at best, or start an all out battle at worse.<br /> <br /> Now, to answer a few comments on the matter<br /> <br /> Yes, as a member of the garou nation, Sargon is supposed to be acting for his sept and caern<br /> <br /> Howether, we talk about an individual here, not a lawful good paladin just out of character creation.<br /> <br /> Garous can doubt their loyalties, and Sargon did. Like many glass walkers, he saw his sept mates as a bunch of anachronistic idiots who still try to resolve an issue doing the same thing with no results.<br /> <br /> That was the starting point of his interest in other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Plus, he didn't &quot;choose the enemy over the garous&quot;,<br /> <br /> To paraphrase his player explaining his actions: &quot;imagine you have two friends, and one of the start beating the other. Of course, you try to stop the one doing the beating, but that does not mean you choosed one over the other, you just stop the agressive one&quot;<br /> <br /> In the same way, Sargon saw his action as protecting his vampiric friends agaisnt his fellow garous. He didn't wanted his septmates to be wounded or killed, but he saw no other options.<br /> <br /> As for the others, they didn't cared.<br /> <br /> They befriended Sargon, the sept for them was just a bunch of garou, a bunch of garou that were going to kill their friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, Henrich was mentioning Nuwisha, and well, it's funny that the table though about the same thing<br /> Here's an in character dialogue between the twin ananasis:<br /> &quot;-No remorse?<br /> -None, their defenses were weak, they were putting too much trust in a single kinfolk, their link with their guardian spirit was based on lies, and their leaders were unable to deal with the situation.<br /> <br /> -well, since they still live, they might learn from this massive faillure, in a way, we helped them, don't you think?<br /> <br /> -...... Oh. Now I think I know how those damn coyotes feel&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T21:06:04-07:00","id":1485451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485418#post1485418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With apologies to Nyremne, because I fully support their choice to make the game more fun for their group even if I didn't necessarily like the resolution.<br /> <br /> In addition to your excellent takedown of the whole spy and oath angle, there's a whole different tone in Nyremne's story about what Sargon actually thinks about the vampires. In the first post it's &quot;they're his friends even if he doesn't admit it&quot; and in the second post &quot;he realises that he's not going to fuck over his friends&quot;. Sargon is a very specific character who is setting his own personal preferences in front of his own Sept and Caern, he doesn't really care for them and cares more for the Enemy than he does for the Caern.<br /> <br /> Also (this may be a personal trauma speaking), but it seems to me that the player doesn't care about the implications or the cultural context, and was actually looking for a way to do his own thing and prove his attitude correct. I feel this is compounded by the willingness to actually threaten the rest of the cast due to his need to &quot;Fight the System&quot;. If he was an actual member of the sept, he'd have some kind of emotions and loyalty to them, as it stands, he was clearly out to show his individualism and devil may care attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure I understand what you mean by cultural impact, could your precise your though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T23:56:38-07:00","id":1485457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these quotes assumes one thing - Sargon has pre-existing obligations to his vampires that the spirits and the Garou have to accept. I don't think that is the case (and if it is, it's a major problem).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from what I read in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>'s post, Sargon did warn the contacts (and only those) with the intend to protect them - not with the intend to screw the Garou and aid the Wyrm. That he might have been naive about that is undisputed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, what do handlers owe the spies they are handling? Usually the answer is nothing. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. And this makes running spies an unhonorable business, possibly. But we don't know how the contacts/allies in Sargons background came to be his informants. Spy stories are full of handlers wanting to rescue their informants (or the relatives of them who survived a botched operation, all the time (Homeland and NCIS NO are the first that come to mind, because I recently watched them)). Also, it doesn't seem like me that Sargon had the &quot;How to be a spy handler&quot; course at the CIA or Shadow Lord sept of your choice. He simply did it, and the sept's members knew about it, but felt uncomfortable to talk about it or set ground rules. I mean, the attack play (despite the Elders hat form vamps) was news to Sargon seemingly, and he wasn't very integrated into the sept, iirc Nyremne's explanations above.<br /> <br /> Having vampire friends in the first place is possibly grounds for the &quot;Wrongful upbringing&quot; Flaw right there. And I would have warned any player that this would not be tolerated if found out. But the game Nyremne is running seemingly had an approach where the sept avoided to deal with this, despite being common knowledge, until it was to late. Not how I see the WtA setting, but I can entertain this approach, based on some 1st Edition TB information on vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, let's assume he did make actual oaths to some vampires. That would be sufficiently troublesome. Many septs won't have a problem if some Garou maintain some kind of contact with the enemy in order to gather intelligence. That does not mean they are sanctioning said Garou to offer oaths with them that conflict with their obligations to the sept.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Which means, that regardless of actual oaths or just mutual understandings, Sarons supervisor failed. Possibly, because he didn't have one. He was somewhat distant to the sept's regular affairs, iirc. That reads to me, as if the sept let him run an autonomous off-the-books operation that backfired eventually, because of lack of oversight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most obvious response to a defense where Sargon talked about the oaths he made to a Wyrm minion should be, &quot;What????? Why did you make an oath to a vampire? When did this happen, and what specifically did you promise them? What other oaths did you make to our enemies?&quot; Those questions would not be to determine if Sargon is guilty, as admitting this just condemned him. It would be to discover the extent of the damage done so the sept knows how they might be compromised so they can take appropriate actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument would be, that someone should have asked these questions months, if not years, prior and course correct Sargon's actions, instead of feeling not responsible while gaining Glory from operations based on intel Sargon provided.<br /> <br /> That said, there are 1st Edition TBs that imply agreements between garou and vampire authorities regarding territories, Masquerade/Veil, mortals and such. So, while I wouldn't handle it this way in my game, I can entertain the idea that the sept allowed Sargon to handle such affairs and didn't really want to know about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485409#post1485409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, let's say Sargon's personal reasons override his duties to the sept, and he wants to save his informants. What is the best thing he can do? It's not what he actually did - tell them of the attack, because that might lead them to inform others (which they did). Instead, a better option would have been to say, &quot;Hey, something important has come up, and I have to explain to you in person. Meet me at this location at this time, and I'll tell you all about it. Once you're there, you'll know why I can't do it over the phone.&quot; Or something to that effect. Maybe it's not to meet Sargon, but some other important contact bringing the vampires evidence of something. Whatever is needed to convince them to go. And whatever time and location would place his informants far away from the scene of the attack. He's gotten them out of there to safety while not compromising any Garou plans. To not do this, but embark on a plan that exploded the sept's plans was a major blunder. And at some point, negligence can become criminal negligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No argument there. He should have known that warning his informants would mean warning all vampires. Bringing them out of harms way under a false pretence would have been much smarter.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also think, that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> is correct, that the character (and possibly the Player's mindset) are set to be &quot;against the system&quot;, meaning garou culture. But that is okay, if you play a mixed-fera-game.<br /> I mean, that is the whole point. Things should have been very different and the setting very different if all the PCs were part of the sept and garou. But then Sargon would have had oversight by the other characters, basically, and they probably would have been stricter if they were garou rather than other fera. Unless the other character were as far away from what we expect garou to be like as Sargon is, but that would be a whole different setting of &quot;against the system&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:24:16-07:00","id":1485467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485451#post1485451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand what you mean by cultural impact, could your precise your though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically; If Sargon was a rited garou, he should know well why vampires are not friends. They are of the Wyrm and are spreading taint even if unintentionally.<br /> <br /> As for the Fera thing, while some see only good garou as dead garou, most want to stay out of the situation. And even the anti-garou ones would not try to sacrifice a holy place of Gaia for one garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:26:13-07:00","id":1485468,"title":"","content":"I mean....your chronicle, your rules but in mine? After that clusterfuck?<br /> <br /> The Corax is going to get ripped to shreds at the next Parliament....verbally.....and possibly physically considering their involvement in endangering a Caern. The Bubasti can probably get away with things as long as they keep their mouth shut at the next Taghairm and don't mention their involvement....if they mention they endangered a Caern? Toast...the Sept the Bastet won't care about but the Cats would be keenly aware that a single one of those cops being Tainted or otherwise having contact with a Bane means part of Gaia dies. The Ananasi.......well...if they are Kumoti they may have to make a minor accounting but otherwise Hatar, Tenere and Antara are either not going to care for the most part or, for some, be actively lauded that a Caern was put in danger.<br /> <br /> Now the Ronin? Because he is 100% a Ronin now, Cockroach is not gonna claim the idiot. He's dead. He's got nowhere to go except the Spirals or a particularly friendly group of kinfolk who are very interested in his hair care routine and carry a lot of knives.....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:06:10-07:00","id":1485479,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out, that cops came to the place they kept Sargon prisoner, not necessarily the Heart of the Caern, Shrines of the Fallen, Gathering Grounds, Guest Quarters or what ever other significant places the Caern Bawn housed. We don't know the specifics about the size of the Bawn and the legalities involved (like did the cops see cult members flee and therefore started to search the area, is the area public or private grounds the cops would have no business entering if there wasn't a reason like pursuit of suspects or a person in distress and so on).<br /> <br /> And sure, if there was a cop with a bane connection, then the cop still would have a need to somehow feel the presence of a caern. Setting is vague on how humans can feel a caern. A cop who somehow is tainted (not corrupted) wouldn't be a problem in any case. I mean, Taint can be acquired by simply taking witness statements from a rape victim and stuff like that. But the Taint vs. Corruption discussion is a whole different topic.<br /> <br /> But again, why wouldn't banes already know where caerns are? I mean, it is these places where gaian spirits are more frequent and more powerful and garou rip banes to shreds when coming close. For hunters, vampires, mages and fae it makes sense that they don't know specifically where caerns are, although some have powers to find them, specifically mages (Prime, Correspondence, no need to even leave the Sanctum). But for Banes and BSD, they have vague ideas on where the garous are (regionally) and therefore their caerns. Unless they tortured a garou for information they might not know the location down to a square meter, but the general area - please...<br /> <br /> Also, I'd say &quot;no, unless the proper Rite is performed, Sargon is most likely still a Glass Walker&quot;. Cockroach accepted him at the end of the Rite of Passage and that's it. I'm not saying that a Incarnae can't remove a garou of the tribe, but they rarely should get involved directly and therefore not do this. There is precedence for traitorous, even wyrmish, garou within septs. 'When will you Rage', for example. Tribal Totems aren't to micromanage their tribes. They have vast powers, but they are neither omnipotent, nor all-knowing, nor having exceptional foresight - hell, some aren't even benevolent.<br /> Plot elements about justice would be pointless, if the garou could always divert their decisions to their supernatural patron, and therefore by extension to the ST.<br /> <br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26564\" data-vbnamecard=\"26564\">BadFurryFanFic</a>, your chronicle, your rules. But there are counter arguments you might want to consider <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T05:07:54-07:00","id":1485488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485468#post1485468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean....your chronicle, your rules but in mine? After that clusterfuck?<br /> <br /> The Corax is going to get ripped to shreds at the next Parliament....verbally.....and possibly physically considering their involvement in endangering a Caern. The Bubasti can probably get away with things as long as they keep their mouth shut at the next Taghairm and don't mention their involvement....if they mention they endangered a Caern? Toast...the Sept the Bastet won't care about but the Cats would be keenly aware that a single one of those cops being Tainted or otherwise having contact with a Bane means part of Gaia dies. The Ananasi.......well...if they are Kumoti they may have to make a minor accounting but otherwise Hatar, Tenere and Antara are either not going to care for the most part or, for some, be actively lauded that a Caern was put in danger.<br /> <br /> Now the Ronin? Because he is 100% a Ronin now, Cockroach is not gonna claim the idiot. He's dead. He's got nowhere to go except the Spirals or a particularly friendly group of kinfolk who are very interested in his hair care routine and carry a lot of knives.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same.<br /> <br /> And to think I've always been the 'softer' ST among WtA players round here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T07:00:40-07:00","id":1485499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485479#post1485479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plot elements about justice would be pointless, if the garou could always divert their decisions to their supernatural patron, and therefore by extension to the ST.<br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26564\" data-vbnamecard=\"26564\">BadFurryFanFic</a>, your chronicle, your rules. But there are counter arguments you might want to consider <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best point you make, and I appreciate your talent and willingness to do mental gymnastics to see the other side of everything. That was also what I could respect about your playstyle back when your Philodox character was still alive and visiting our Sept.<br /> <br /> But when you argue that &quot;Hey it's the WoD, there are cults everywhere, getting one police station on the tracks of one abduction might not be that big of a deal as some in this forum think&quot;, I ask you what those PC would have to do even worse for you to accept it as a problem for the Veil?<br /> <br /> And when you argue that &quot;Leading the attention of cops to the Bawn&quot; (in combination with an abduction [and hints towards a cult] you will get not only the attention of street-level cops, that's where you get the detective-level equivalent of french cops involved. Also cops don't get the order to rush in anywhere to get an abduction victim out without at least one judge in the next bigger city deciding, exponentially increasing the number of potential supernaturals who get a copy of those informations) is not enough to judge that as endangering a Caern, in which way would the PCs of at least the GW and the Corax (and maybe the Bastet) need to behave worse than they did for you to judge it as knowingly endangering a Caern?<br /> <br /> I am repeating myself, but just have a look on the satellite pictures of europe (not implying that their Lille has to copy our real-world-Lille, just as a general thought that we're not talking about siberia here). This is the old world, there are human buildings everywhere. Even the centers of the biggest pieces of forest aren't out of range for a walk on a sunday afternoon.You wouldn't want that kind of attention for the Caern of your Larp-Sept, would you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T10:22:25-07:00","id":1485519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485479#post1485479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd say &quot;no, unless the proper Rite is performed, Sargon is most likely still a Glass Walker&quot;. Cockroach accepted him at the end of the Rite of Passage and that's it. I'm not saying that a Incarnae can't remove a garou of the tribe, but they rarely should get involved directly and therefore not do this. There is precedence for traitorous, even wyrmish, garou within septs. 'When will you Rage', for example. Tribal Totems aren't to micromanage their tribes. They have vast powers, but they are neither omnipotent, nor all-knowing, nor having exceptional foresight - hell, some aren't even benevolent.<br /> Plot elements about justice would be pointless, if the garou could always divert their decisions to their supernatural patron, and therefore by extension to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with this. The Incarna have always been presented as rather distant. Even the Jaggling Avatars of Incarna are just an aspect of them and don't like to spend any more time than necessary on more prosaic reality. When the Incarna &quot;speak&quot; it should usually be in omens and dreams that need to be interpreted with lots of uncertainty to their meaning. It's best to let the Garou NPCs handle things when it come to things like this. Plus, no matter how bad Sargon screwed up, there's been plenty of Garou down the centuries who have done much, much, much worse. Nightmaster in the Abyss is clearly Wyrm tainted and committing atrocities, yet he's still a Shadow Lord, not a Ronin.<br /> <br /> Plus, when it comes to matters of right and wrong, players can have very different ideas about these matters. And if an ST comes down from on high and says they are ruling this or that action is objectively wrong, evil, unjust, etc. by the highest powers of the universe, it can bother players in ways that saying &quot;Yeah, this particular group of NPCs ruled what you did was wrong&quot; does not.<br /> <br /> I actually don't have a problem with how the ST or the player of Sargon are choosing to react. Sargon, the character, isn't acting appropriately to Garou customs, but it's all valid choices by the player. As long as everyone is having fun and the game can go on, it's working at the table. It's just that the NPCs should be reacting in a certain way now if you want to adhere more or less with how the setting has been presented. And these actions are turning the game in a direction I don't think anyone expected, and this may cause problems further on down the line. But if everyone is on board with them being fugitives from justice and making their way in the WoD no matter what direction it takes them, then go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-01-2022, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T10:37:30-07:00","id":1485521,"title":"","content":"Absolutely.<br /> Maybe Cockroach wouldn't accept a hypothetical someone who somehow managed to screw up this bad before even having a tribe, but the Totems don't micromanage their Garou like toy soldiers.<br /> Actively throwing someone out of the tribe and declaring him Ronin is something that much rather happens by Garou doing it to each other.<br /> There would be little sense in having a whole Auspice (and a half) being about dealing with judgement (and scandals) when the Spirits would automatically monitor and punish Garou behavior anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:22:49-07:00","id":1485530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485499#post1485499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when you argue that &quot;Hey it's the WoD, there are cults everywhere, getting one police station on the tracks of one abduction might not be that big of a deal as some in this forum think&quot;, I ask you what those PC would have to do even worse for you to accept it as a problem for the Veil?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a storytelling standpoint the Veil is a whole other problem.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Veil shall not be lifted&quot; and each garou has an obligation to reduce any chance that this might happen. But what does that mean?<br /> Bone Gnawers are known to bring humans into the fold who are not blood related to any fera (so no kinfolk in the sense of game mechanics) and Children of Gaia have a Rite to (secretly) turn a human into a kinfolk (something other tribes might see as breach of these Litany Tenet).<br /> And, surely the knowledge that garou exist not a secret kept from other supernaturals, but also (probably) not from lesser supernaturals like sorcerers, psionics, kinain or possibly mediums and the fraction known as Gypsies. All arguably humans.<br /> So, while some Garou would call bringing just one human into the fold was a breach of the Litany, others argue the rule applies to keep the knowledge of the garou away from the general population - but one individual does not constitute a breach.<br /> <br /> Both interpretations have merit, since the Litany is a whole bunch of legends and anecdotal evidence from which the Tenet is derived. According to the earlier DA Werewolf book, this specific Tenet wasn't even in the original Litany but was added in the wake of the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Obviously the ST doesn't want the Veil to be lifted, because it would be a radical change in the Setting. Even if not the general public but only intelligence agencies are aware of the supernatural, it might be a hugely different Setting. I mean, there was Project Twilight and Strike Force Zero in 2nd and revised Edition, but Vampire 5th Edition is a whole new world because of the Masquerade being partly lifted.<br /> <br /> And then there is &quot;Time of Judgement&quot;. Lucifer, the Devil, personally tried to bring Faith into the world on a whole new level - performing real magic for a live audience and basically saving the world. But, the Camarilla and Technocracy ran counter propaganda successfully and the world was doomed.<br /> <br /> But of course garou can't depend on the mages and vamps to save the Veil. But they have Gifts of their own to convince, confuse and alter evidence. They are somewhat limited when it comes to altering memories (apart from the human reaction to the Delirium which is also called Veil).<br /> <br /> The thing is, how would the cops when they come to save Sargon learn about the supernatural existing and werewolves being real?<br /> Would the garou of the sept sit around in Crinos form for the body cams of the cops to record? Do cops in France even have body cams? I watched &quot;The Rookie&quot; a lot, since it became available on Disney+ in Germany. In Germany cops don't have those in general. SEKs (which are SWAT-like response units) might have, though.<br /> Do the garou of the sept have &quot;Hello, I'm a werewolf&quot;-buttons to wear on their shirts? I think not.<br /> <br /> Even with the Kin who normally deters the cops from the sept there should be spirit-, kin- and garou guardians who would notice the police arriving. And while some garou might suspect corrupt cops, wyrm minions and such and therefore elect to kill them pre-emptively (which would for sure escalate the situation with reinforcements being called and so on) there might also be other garou who would elect to hide as many non socially oriented sept members as they can and employ Gifts to confuse or bullshit their way out of the situation with magical eloquence.<br /> &quot;You know, officer, this guy is mad at us, for we don't want him in our society. He probably chained himself up in that shag after he called you.&quot;<br /> Backed by Persuasion, Spellbinding Oration or even Ultimate Logical Argument, if available.<br /> <br /> Sure, calling the cops to the Bawn is reckless. But as far as the Veil is concerned, there are a lot of things imaginable that are far more threatening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485499#post1485499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when you argue that &quot;Leading the attention of cops to the Bawn&quot; (in combination with an abduction [and hints towards a cult] you will get not only the attention of street-level cops, that's where you get the detective-level equivalent of french cops involved. Also cops don't get the order to rush in anywhere to get an abduction victim out without at least one judge in the next bigger city deciding, exponentially increasing the number of potential supernaturals who get a copy of those informations) is not enough to judge that as endangering a Caern, in which way would the PCs of at least the GW and the Corax (and maybe the Bastet) need to behave worse than they did for you to judge it as knowingly endangering a Caern?</div> </div> </div> </div>Endangering the Caern is a whole different story from the Veil.<br /> <br /> There are mentions of lost caerns in the world. Even if all garou were to be arrested, the caern would not be harmed by that. Neither by the presence of humans.<br /> <br /> Generally it is not clear how fragile caerns are, what is considered a desecration, and all that. We only know that Gatherings have to be performed monthly and significant Gnosis need to be invested. But, like I said, there are mentions of lost caerns not attended by for centuries.<br /> <br /> Like I wrote above, there is an argument being made that some supernatural factions already have an idea where a caern is. Those who don't might not get the information just from the police reports.<br /> <br /> The leap from police report about a cult and an abduction, to garou, to sacred place inhabited by garou is highly circumstantial. I mean if the Veil is preserved the police report doesn't even go into the Garou direction. Cults that abduct people could be Sabbat, Wyrm Cults like the 7th Generation, Sorcerer groups, changelings or student groups or any other strange cabal. For all the police knows, a hiker called in the BDSM enthusiasts having rented a house in the woods.<br /> Depending on the specific information in the call, we don't know.<br /> <br /> Leading Wyrm beasts to the caern, or any other faction that in known or suspected to harm caerns intentionally is another situation. But human cops at the bawn far less threatening. Sure, there could be dire consequences, but are they really likely?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485499#post1485499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am repeating myself, but just have a look on the satellite pictures of europe (not implying that their Lille has to copy our real-world-Lille, just as a general thought that we're not talking about siberia here). This is the old world, there are human buildings everywhere. Even the centers of the biggest pieces of forest aren't out of range for a walk on a sunday afternoon.You wouldn't want that kind of attention for the Caern of your Larp-Sept, would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as a ST I would give players ways to deflect attention away from the caern again, if the police was ever called to the caern for some reason. That said, whenever we come to play, we do howls all the time. Do the people in the village come investigate? No, they don't. Because they know that there is a camping site the scout organisation rents out for all kinds of events.<br /> <br /> The same is true for the sept in our setting. The Kin who was usually deflecting such attention by the police away from the caern (who was removed by the Ananasi in this case) would have had a story spun over the years downplaying all other ominous calls about the sept, just like there certainly is some cover story that the humans tell amongst themselves about the strange people that are there in the woods.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. Calling the cops is a dangerous gamble and it was done for selfish reasons, that surely warrants a punishment. But things aren't as dire as depicted here. Just imagine, if a lost cub was part of the sept and due to that Flaw the parents of that cub don't accept that their child is now living in the woods for no apparent reason called the cops on that cult that abducted their child. Would the cub be executed for that? Or the Den Parent, as the person responsible for the cubs?<br /> Have caerns ever been violated by that?<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> wrote, at some point negligence becomes criminal negligence. But to really judge the circumstances there are a lot of questions about the Setting that have to be cleared first. Like how fragile is a caern, how close was the prison shack to the rest of the caern infrastructure, what guardians were in place to shield the sept of the approaching police, what does the local population know or think to be true about the sept and so on.<br /> That is, judging from an outside standpoint. For the sept members it is clearly a totally emotional situation and they might have totally different ideas about punishment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-01-2022, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:16:55-07:00","id":1485563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485439#post1485439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think I went soft on them, the npcs acted in a way that was consistent with their character and the situation, the players took great risks and are clearly not out of trouble.<br /> <br /> For now, we don't know where they're going, we ended the session right after Sargon's situation, the players are discussing running away through the umbra, leaving the continent, or trying to find a spirit of deception to mask Sargon's identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>When things got really serious and Sargon was willing to go full asshole on the Caern you let it slide. Not only did you let him live beyond that but actively supressed anyone reacting to it then and there in a frenzy or simply challenging him for the insult he has brought upon them. After that you intentionally left him alive in a place that was easy to get to by the rest of the cast, and which ordinary humans could get into and get him out with zero interference from about 20 Garou you just said were around and who could have used any kind of gifts to belay them or simply tell the cops to fuck off. Sure you played it all as a comedy and leaned into the atmosphere your players wanted, but you really, really went easy on Sargon as a player and the group for their solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485439#post1485439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also qay that I don't think I've retconned the setting or that the player of Sargon acted in a selfish manner</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485439#post1485439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand what you mean by cultural impact, could your precise your though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the whole feel from your presentation is that the Sept is a bunch of hypocritical buffoons. They are clearly the butt of a Nuwisha level joke. Not sure if that was your goal, maybe it was if you were leaning into some kind of Fera brotherhood versus Garou bigotry, but considering that you have two manipulative psychopats in the party most likely using the group for their ends in the party I'm not so sure.<br /> <br /> So far you have presented Sargon as a character that belongs to that Caern and to that Sept. Not just that, but he's not even an outsider there - he has a lot of friends and connections (werewolf and otherwise) and he has managed to get to Rank 2. This means that he is well versed in Garou societal norms and behavior, that he is a genuine part of this culture. Considering what he was allowed before things went to hell, he was clearly a respected and trusted member of this society. Better yet, he had roots - most likely some family, mentors, friends, maybe even packmates?<br /> <br /> None of that is visible from his interactions. He is selfish, doesn't care about the society that he belongs to and seems driven by antagonism and spite.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T23:45:30-07:00","id":1485605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485563#post1485563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far you have presented Sargon as a character that belongs to that Caern and to that Sept. Not just that, but he's not even an outsider there - he has a lot of friends and connections (werewolf and otherwise) and he has managed to get to Rank 2. This means that he is well versed in Garou societal norms and behavior, that he is a genuine part of this culture.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement#post1485044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sargon is a fostern (rank 2) from the glasswalker tribe. He's a member of the local cairn, even though he rarely interact with it's members outside of meetings and other important occasions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyremne's quote is from the very first post. So, I never got the impression that Sargon is a sept member integrated into the sept and well connected with the local garou.<br /> <br /> I mean, he wasn't even aware of the planned attack until right before it was about to happen. The Elders didn't seek his counsel, albeit him being the expert on the local leeches. Why not? Because they didn't care - leeches are of the Wyrm and need to be eradicated. Maybe they were disgusted about themselves for letting the whole Sargon situation slide for too long.<br /> <br /> Possibly the Sargon got Fostern rank simply be accumulation of renown over a long period of time. Still, none of the sept members (at least not the important ones) realised his lack of conviction towards garou society/cultural standards.<br /> <br /> If Sargon was really well integrated, would have had stronger acquaintances with the local garou instead of just with the fera and leeches, the whole situation could have been avoided.<br /> <br /> Like I said above, Sargon is not a good handler for vampire contacts, as e is left unsupervised for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-02-2022, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T15:11:54-07:00","id":1485655,"title":"","content":"He has two elders covering for him. Why? Doesn't that clearly show he is a valued member trusted by the most senior members? You don't get that kind of trust without playing by their rules and being someone they can trust. So yes, he's quite hooked into it on paper. He just doesn't give a damn in practice preferring his non Garou contacts and leading me back to the fact that the player is intentionally downplaying the culture and millleau he belongs to to make a statement and embrace what they feel is the right way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T16:03:22-07:00","id":1485660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485655#post1485655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has two elders covering for him. Why? Doesn't that clearly show he is a valued member trusted by the most senior members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> stated the Sept Leader (Fianna, Elder) had in the past turned a blind eye but was out of patience. Erebus instead of execution is something he might quickly agree before a long debate sheds too much light on how he mishandled the Sargon situation in the past.<br /> The Glass Walker Elder seemingly was always on Sargons side, having in the past shielded him from earlier accusation of being treacherous. We don't know his motivations. Is he simply helping him because of tribal companionship? Is he his secret father? What ever the reason - this is the one actively covering for him.<br /> <br /> One could argue that Erebus is a fate worst than death, since it is most often deadly, but death is only after torture and humiliation, so....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485655#post1485655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get that kind of trust without playing by their rules and being someone they can trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't necessarily trust him. The Glass Walker has misplaced loyalties or a motivation we don't know (maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> can elaborate), but he knew of earlier accusations and shielded Sargon. Maybe he thought Sargon and his dealing were beneficial enough to go through such lengths. Or maybe he thought that he had to protect the Glass Walker tribal reputation by downplaying all of Sargons earlier failings instead of admitting that his tribesman was doing wrongful things.<br /> Until Nyremne elaborates, we can only speculate why this NPC was mishandling the Sargon situation so dramatically.<br /> <br /> As for the Fianna Septleader. He is an example for criminally negligent. He has turned a blind eye, most likely to avoid internal trouble with his Co-Elder, or because he didn't care. If his Co-Elder was so eager to defend Sargon's failures, he possibly even got some considerations by the Glass Walker Elder for not opposing him in his hobby of being Sargon's advocate. But he doesn't trust Sargon. He might even hate him. Like I said, agreeing to Erebus instead of execution might just have been a political move.<br /> <br /> The third elder agreeing probably is also due to internal political circumstances in the dynamic of the three Elders. Still, the need to kill the vampire friends to show that there is really a possibility of redemption is a nice move to wheat out the bullshit the Glass Walker Elder is selling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485044-incoming-judgement?p=1485655#post1485655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, he's quite hooked into it on paper. He just doesn't give a damn in practice preferring his non Garou contacts and leading me back to the fact that the player is intentionally downplaying the culture and millleau he belongs to to make a statement and embrace what they feel is the right way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd lean towards the player having chosen and imagined Sargon as an outsider within the sept intentionally, so that he can downplay the culture and better fit in with the other PCs, which are Fera. Intentionally trying to belong to the sept as little as possible, within the confines of the chronicle.<br /> I mean, the game is a Fera chronicle, not a WtA game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-02-2022, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}